  "body": "Found while working #731 (PR #1361, `mcp_setup_moves`).\n\nWhat happens: delete a setup that is not the last one, then undo. The setup comes back at the END of the setup list, not at the position it was deleted from. The setup order is the machining order and the order setups post in, so after an undo the program order silently differs from what it was before the delete.\n\nExpected: Everything Is a Command means undo restores the previous state, and that includes the setup's position.\n\nEvidence: `crates/app/tests/mcp_setup_moves.rs` (PR #1361) has to compare the setup names sorted because of this. The same command runs from the GUI's Setups page.\n\nDone means: undoing `DeleteSetup` puts the setup back at its index, and a test deletes a middle setup, undoes, and pins the order, plus the posted program order if setups post in sequence.\n",
